{
  "analysis": "The VM is now well understood: little-endian MIPS, word-addressed memory, loads ELF sections .text/.data/.rodata by name, uses the `main` symbol as entry point, and uses x86/Linux syscall numbers (read=0, write=1, open=2, close=3, lseek=8, time=201). No FPU support is apparent. A freestanding mipsel build with a minimal libc/syscall shim and soft-float is required. The mipsel cross-compiler is installed.",
  "plan": "Inspect the doomgeneric_img.c includes and verify the toolchain. Then I'll create a minimal libc with syscall wrappers using x86 syscall numbers, a bump allocator, and minimal stdio/string functions. After that, compile all doomgeneric C files with the custom platform file and link as a static freestanding MIPS ELF.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '1,40p' /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/doomgeneric_img.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/*.c | wc -l\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "command -v mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc && mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc --version | head -2\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
